Z||000018||FieroHeather||07-26-2001||01:08 AM||||I like tea.  I grew up having "tea time" with my grandfather who was Canadian-English every day in the summertime (when off from school).  I liked LOTS of milk and LOTS of sugar to hide the tea taste.  I was 8, give me a break  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>When I got into High School, I really liked Hot Chocolate.  That was the way to go.  I actually started drinking Iced Tea (Lipton's Original flavor, not Lemon Flavor) just because my crush drank it.  I found out that if I poured some of my lunchtime's milk into the ice tea bottle, I could drink it faster, and I liked the taste better.  Gross, I know!  But I had to impress my crush!!<P>Oh...teenagers, eh? !!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>When in College, I got into the whole hang out scene with tea.  I miss my best friend dearly.  He and I would have "tea time" like once a week or so.  It was one of those intimate times where you could talk about anything that you wanted to, and you still felt accepted  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Man, I miss that!!<P>My Hot chocolate phase was re-kindled when those flavored kinds came out (Mint, and English Toffee)... My new mutual crush loved drinking Hot Chocolate with me (while he had coffee), but it was the company that mattered, not so much the drink.  Tim Hortons was our best place to hang out!  However, the Earl Grey made by my best friend still beat out the Hot Chocolate dates.  He put TONS of sugar in it for me--but NO milk was allowed.  His rule.  <P>Me?  I got into the herbal teas, especially the mint tea flavour.  I feel special drinking tea, cause it reminds me of who Heather is and who I was  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||7
Z||000019||Philphine||07-26-2001||01:38 AM||||in the summer or really any time if i'm not drinking lemonade i'm drinking lemon tea. sometimes in the winter i drink it hot. favorite hot is scoop out the juice and pulp from half a grape fruit and lots of sugar in a big mug of tea. sounds wierd i know but i love it.  <P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>SERENITY NOW!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000020||Patrick's Dad||07-26-2001||09:36 AM||||Cool that so many love tea!<P>88CoupeV6: I dicovered Tealuxe on Newbury Street (Not pretentious, just going from the Hynes to the Public Gardens on my way to Park Street Sta. and then home!) Their tea has been very good to me, esp. Russian Caravan and the Darjeeling White (although the latter is expensive!)<P>My wife just found an item in the Weymouth News that there's going to be a demonstration of the Japanese Tea Ceremony at the Duxbury Art Complex Museum at 2:00 this Sunday. Have to do inventory until noon, but am going to try to make it.||||reg||10
